    {
        "content": "<p>Haven't checked the example yet, but be aware that there is a distinction between \"assumption X is unused\" and \"proof still compiles without assumption X\", especially if X is a type-class argument. EDIT: This is not the issue here.</p>",
        "id": 612371484,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1784816618
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Making <code>foo'</code> a public lemma triggers the linter.<br>\nI think this is an example of something I've said before: We haven't adapted much of the Mathlib (and Batteries, I guess) meta-code to the module system yet.</p>",
        "id": 612372028,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1784816748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I do think the unused arguments linter (and most/all other linters) should trigger on private declarations: if private lemma <code>X</code> has an unused argument, chances are that public lemma <code>Y</code> that uses <code>X</code> also has an unused argument.</p>",
        "id": 612372582,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1784816887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"548935\">@Thomas Murrills</span> Do you know if <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/pull/1831\">batteries#1831</a> will fix this? (Reading through the code, it seems to me the answer will be yes... but I didn't realize this until now.)</p>",
        "id": 612378219,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1784818195
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yep, that should fix it! :)</p>",
